{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ties."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that strict order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the minimum spanning forest is unique, and this is it, whichever algorithm runs: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canonical forest, listed in nondecreasing weight and, among equal weights, in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, with the weight added up in that order. Currently Kruskal’s algorithm on sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) and otherwise Prim’s under that order followed by a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sort of the n − 1 edges taken, which is faster on denser graphs (see the benchmarks)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop, never for a self-loop, and not kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights, and so are infinities. A NaN weight traps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NetworkX instead offers ","type":"text"},{"code":"ignore_nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; filter such edges out first).","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m log m).","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not overflow and is not NaN.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","symbolKind":"method","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Kruskal.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L24"},"modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component (NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and igraph’s "},{"code":"minimum_spanning_tree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/Graph